{"thought": "Now I understand the vulnerability clearly:

In `pgp_parse_algo_attr_blob`, the `oid.value` array has `SC_MAX_OBJECT_ID_OCTETS = 16` entries (each is an `int`, so 4 bytes each = 64 bytes total).

The vulnerable loop:
```c
for (j=0; j < (blob->len-1); j++) {
    oid.value[j] = blob->data[j+1];
}
```

If `blob->len - 1 > 16`, this writes past the end of `oid.value`, causing a stack buffer overflow. The crash type confirms "Stack-buffer-overflow WRITE 4" (4 bytes = size of int).

Now I need to understand what the fuzz harness looks like to craft an appropriate input."}
